# Mintlify deployment (T3Planet Docs)

Live site: https://docs.t3planet.de/en/latest  
Mintlify project: **T3Planet Docs** (workspace **nitsan-81630f36**)

## Connected GitHub (source of live builds)

**Use only the org repository** for deployment:

- Live / deploy source: **`nitsan-technologies/T3Planet-docs`** branch `master`
- Local remote name: **`origin`** → `https://github.com/nitsan-technologies/T3Planet-docs.git`

Do **not** use `markus-neumannn/T3Planet-docs` as the normal deploy target.

Mintlify dashboard **Git** settings must point at **`nitsan-technologies/T3Planet-docs`** (`master`). If Git settings still show the Markus fork, live will not follow `origin` pushes — reconnect Git in the Mintlify dashboard.

### Author vs repository (do not confuse)

- **Commit author:** always **Markus** `<248457632+markus-neumannn@users.noreply.github.com>`
- **Push remote:** always **`origin`** → `nitsan-technologies/T3Planet-docs`
- Markus **name** ≠ Markus **fork repo**

### Emergency live unblock (2026-09-23 lesson)

If the user needs live **now** and Mintlify Activity still shows `markus-neumannn/T3Planet-docs`:

1. Prefer reconnecting Mintlify Git to the org repo.
2. If reconnect is blocked and live is urgent: temporarily `git remote add markus …`, `git push markus origin/master:master` (same SHA already on org), poll live until content matches, then `git remote remove markus`.
3. Tell the user clearly this was an emergency sync because Mintlify Git was still on the fork.

For normal releases:

1. Commit as Markus (email above).
2. `git push origin HEAD:master`
3. Confirm Mintlify **Activity** + spot-check live HTML (not HTTP 200 alone).

Full procedure: see repo root `context.md`.

